# zhoda-core conventions

- Python 3.12+, `uv` for deps, src layout: `core/src/zhoda_core/`.
- Pydantic v2 models live in `models/` and must mirror the schemas in
  docs/01-core.md: ValueMap, Position, Critique, FactionSwitch, Verdict,
  Disagreement, CostReport. Changing a schema = update the doc in the same commit.
- All model calls are async (`httpx.AsyncClient`). Fan-out via
  `asyncio.gather(return_exceptions=True)`: a failed model is excluded from the
  round; raise only if ALL models failed (graceful degradation).
- No blocking I/O inside async functions. No `time.sleep` — use `asyncio.sleep`.
- OpenRouter provider: retries with exponential backoff on 429/5xx, semantic
  cache keyed by hash(question + value_map + model), strict JSON parsing of
  model outputs with one repair retry.
- Type hints everywhere; `ruff` + `mypy` clean. Line length 100.
- Tests: pytest, recorded fixtures only (no live API calls in CI). Three
  canonical scenarios: consensus, split, escalation.
- CLI entry: `zhoda deliberate "..."` (typer), live round output via rich.
